# CYS-CAA-mod2-chloride — alternative mod2 for the chloride pre-reaction input
#
# When the user uploaded a ligand with the Cl still drawn (the free
# drug SMILES form, e.g. ClCC(=O)N1CCN(C1)…), this mod2 REPLACES the
# default `data_mod_CYS-CAA-mod2` in CYS-CAA.cif. Encodes the SN2
# substitution chemistry:
#
#   (1) Delete the Cl atom and its bond to Cβ
#   (2) Cβ retypes from "sp3 C with halogen" to "sp3 C with thioether"
#       — same CT energy type, slightly different partial charge
#       environment. Coot's bond perception draws this from the atom
#       type so the visible result is correct without explicit retype.
#   (3) The new SG-Cβ bond is added via the link's bond block (not here)
#
# No H is added on Cβ in this mod — F3 SN2 doesn't add a hydrogen
# (unlike F1/F2 Michael addition, which transfers a proton to Cα).
# The Cl just leaves and S takes its place; Cβ keeps its existing 2 H's.
#
# Selected at runtime when the SMARTS detector matched CYS-CAA-pre
# (chloroacetamide-bearing ligand, R-N-C(=O)-CH₂-Cl).
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime:
#   <CB>  ← attack-site C atom-id (the α-methylene C)
#   <CL>  ← Cl atom-id to delete
#
# References:
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/covalent-ligand-plan.md §2.3
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/refs/nicholls-modelling-2021.pdf §3.1 (chem_mod semantics)

data_mod_CYS-CAA-mod2

# (1) Delete the Cβ-Cl bond
loop_
_chem_mod_bond.mod_id
_chem_mod_bond.function
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_mod_bond.new_type
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist_esd
 CYS-CAA-mod2 delete <CB> <CL> . . .

# (2) Delete the Cl atom itself
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-CAA-mod2 delete <CL> . . . .
